    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s iconic Barrackville Covered Bridge, built in 1853, is the second‑oldest covered bridge in West Virginia and spans Buffalo Creek.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://wvexplorer.com/communities/cities-towns/barrackville-west-virginia/"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In the early 1900s, Barrackville became a coal hub when the Jamison Coal & Coke Company built a mining camp for its workers.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23,
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://wvexplorer.com/communities/cities-towns/barrackville-west-virginia/"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The community sits two miles northwest of Fairmont in the Monongahela Valley, placing it near the West Fork River watershed.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        27,
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://wvexplorer.com/communities/cities-towns/barrackville-west-virginia/"
    },
    {
